<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>BBC News</title><subtitle type="html">BBC News - Technology</subtitle><id>https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/technology/rss.xml</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:36:50Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss.xml" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/technology" /><link rel="via" href="https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/technology/rss.xml" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Courts, spies and MPs: How the Microsoft outage has been felt around the world</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqp9d58eldlro#0</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:35:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T15:44:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqp9d58eldlro--829c82d81c0a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqp9d58eldlro?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">From city governments in the US to spy agencies in Australia, the Microsoft outage is being felt around the world.</summary></entry><entry><title>Bessent blames Lutnick's Commerce Department for failing to block Megaspeed</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqvg2d1eg7zro#0</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:35:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T15:40:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqvg2d1eg7zro--c19561116954.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqvg2d1eg7zro?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Scott Bessent told CNBC that several government agencies "were in favour of putting Megaspeed on the entity list for months".</summary></entry><entry><title>Why is the Microsoft outage lasting so long?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwvg238zrnm5o#0</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:34:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T14:21:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwvg238zrnm5o--f83f812563eb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwvg238zrnm5o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Microsoft says it is seeing "improvements" following a global outage but efforts to fully resume services are ongoing.</summary></entry><entry><title>NHS, schools and police forces hit by Microsoft outage</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6vg2ljjpj32o#0</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:35:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T13:41:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6vg2ljjpj32o--938c3e3c1998.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6vg2ljjpj32o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Major airports and intelligence services are unaffected, while the government is still assessing the impact.</summary></entry><entry><title>How a sex scandal at Nvidia is putting pressure on the White House</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c67429m3vem3o#0</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:34:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T12:22:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c67429m3vem3o--64838ee6839b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c67429m3vem3o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Jensen Huang's personal life may have triggered the crisis, but the questions now reach into the White House itself.</summary></entry><entry><title>What we know so far about the Microsoft outage</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/cqzjr903n01po#0</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:35:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T11:43:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/cqzjr903n01po--82c7a02c8237.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/cqzjr903n01po?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">A Microsoft outage is affecting services including Teams, Outlook and AI software Copilot.</summary></entry><entry><title>Heat pumps: How much heat does your home really need?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqy43zk3kk04o#0</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:36:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T09:29:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqy43zk3kk04o--691a4e74f9e6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqy43zk3kk04o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Knowing how much heat your home loses is important before installing a new heating system.</summary></entry><entry><title>What happened overnight with the Microsoft global outage?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/cwm2591k27e2o#0</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:36:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T07:18:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/cwm2591k27e2o--cfd115ed130a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/cwm2591k27e2o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Microsoft is struggling to fix a global outage, with services including Teams, Outlook and AI software Copilot affected by "connectivity problems".</summary></entry><entry><title>Ex-Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang summoned to testify before Congress about affair with alleged Chinese spy</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmq5vd1wdgz6o#0</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:34:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T03:57:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmq5vd1wdgz6o--607d4d7557c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmq5vd1wdgz6o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Huang abruptly quit on Thursday as head of one of the world's most valuable companies after revelations of alleged extramarital affairs.</summary></entry><entry><title>Global Microsoft outage affecting tens of thousands of users</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c5gm3g9ldz8xo#0</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:34:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T02:38:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c5gm3g9ldz8xo--7d226533f769.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c5gm3g9ldz8xo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Microsoft said the outage was caused by servers unexpected becoming unavailable, straining other systems.</summary></entry><entry><title>The rise of 'housefishing' - when does using AI go from enhancing to misleading?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm62y0wrnz9zo#0</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:34:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T00:13:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm62y0wrnz9zo--e31d579ac014.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm62y0wrnz9zo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Experts warn that using AI to enhance property images can go too far and mislead prospective buyers.</summary></entry><entry><title>The rise and fall of Jensen Huang - how the tech superstar became mired in scandal</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmze750zg0jeo#0</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:34:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T17:11:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmze750zg0jeo--00916c7a76a8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmze750zg0jeo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Within days, Huang's status as a seemingly untouchable figure leading the global tech race has crumbled.</summary></entry><entry><title>How AI visionary Jensen Huang was undone by his own bad decisions</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cq5y13819gpjo#0</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:34:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T16:43:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cq5y13819gpjo--376d5a6f39d9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cq5y13819gpjo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Zoe Kleinman explains how the man who built Nvidia from the ground up lost everything in a matter of days.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tech Life</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyv#2</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:34:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T20:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyv--9798c5d5f4ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyv?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">We investigate internet-connected device flaws worldwide, plus US election tech fallout.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tech Life</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyt#2</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:34:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T20:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyt--974b9860edd3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyt?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">When copyright strikes silence reporters, rail safety &amp; the Lord of the Rings live show.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tech Life</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jys#2</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:34:02Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T20:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jys--8346efbd8e2d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jys?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">We hear from Ondřej Surý, the programmer whose PHP patches h